  "checks": [
    "C11, C++20, CPython and Rust each install an ordinary and a reviewed standalone IO / EIO / BaseIO package. Effects are checked against the filesystem grant. No Task, iterator, or host import is needed.",
    "The installed clients distinguish an actual filesystem IO failure, a thrown EIO error carrying either arm of an owned string/integer result, the same value returned normally (the C++ and Rust clients include an embedded NUL), and a refused host call. Successful calls show ordered state changes and leave no owned identities.",
    "C++ copied-only calls have no dispatcher or task headers in their package. Rust's resolved standalone provider has neither enabled features nor dependencies; async-io, polling and futures-core are absent.",
    "In each mixed-resource client a synchronous component borrows or returns a live Lean Badge, and a real task in an independently installed component mutates and returns the same Badge. Throwing that Badge as a typed error preserves its identity; the error lease remains usable and cloneable. Stale access fails and all leases are released.",
    "The two Rust peers depend on the exact same provider archive. Only the actual task component enables async. The C++ client also checks that invalid cold input opens no dispatcher and that worker-thread disposal is drained on the owner thread."
  ],
  "reproduce": {
    "build": "LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_SYNC_TEST=1 LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_SYNC_EVIDENCE=/absolute/path/to/new-releases node --test --test-concurrency=1 tests/helpers/native-sync-io.mjs",
    "replay": "LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_SYNC_REPLAY=/absolute/path/to/original-releases LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_SYNC_EXPECTED=docs/evidence/native-sync-cpp-rust-20261122.json node --test --test-concurrency=1 tests/helpers/native-sync-io.mjs",
    "buildPeers": "LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_SYNC_MIXED_TEST=1 LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_SYNC_MIXED_EVIDENCE=/absolute/path/to/new-peers node --test --test-concurrency=1 tests/helpers/native-sync-peer.mjs",
    "replayPeers": "LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_SYNC_MIXED_REPLAY=/absolute/path/to/original-peers LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_SYNC_MIXED_EXPECTED=docs/evidence/native-sync-cpp-rust-20261122.json node --test --test-concurrency=1 tests/helpers/native-sync-peer.mjs",
    "tools": "Building requires the pinned Lean installation (LEAN_BRIDGE_LEAN_PREFIX), C/C++ compilers, CMake, pkg-config, CPython headers, and Cargo with an offline crate cache for the pinned lockfiles. Replaying requires the original package sets, consumer toolchains and the offline cache, but no Lean compiler."
  },
